1
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:26,860
Aiming for the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:27,680 --> 00:00:34,000
I kicked a pebble and my shoe flew off too.

3
00:00:34,940 --> 00:00:42,240
Onto the head of the
carpenter I had in a chokehold,

4
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:48,440
they laughed that I was still just a brat.

5
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:55,280
Even if I lose my spirit somewhere else,
Katsushika is worth it.

6
00:00:55,280 --> 00:01:02,540
Yawning once more,
the unchanging streets feel strangely kind.

7
00:01:03,860 --> 00:01:10,440
From the pointed-hat water tower,

8
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:16,780
the sunset sinks into the vast heavens.

9
00:01:20,280 --> 00:01:25,260
Tomorrow will end just like this too,
won't it?

10
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:30,320
Katsushika, Shibamata,
even happiness is lost again.

11
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:33,860
Because I'm a fool who finally realized it.

12
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:40,540
As his older brother,

13
00:01:46,360 --> 00:01:49,060
this is a gift from Mr. Ryotsu.

14
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:51,440
Please accept it and keep
it for many years to come.

15
00:01:56,460 --> 00:01:58,840
What a wonderful honor this is.

16
00:01:59,480 --> 00:02:02,000
Keiko is beautiful,
and she has such a lovely disposition.

17
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,640
She's far too good for Kinjiro!

18
00:02:04,860 --> 00:02:07,720
You charmer, you lucky devil!
How did you trick her?

19
00:02:08,320 --> 00:02:09,980
Dad, you're drinking too much.

20
00:02:10,540 --> 00:02:13,058
Don't be ridiculous, Berubumyun.

21
00:02:13,108 --> 00:02:17,009
When I'm happy, I drink until I drop.
That's the Edokko way.

22
00:02:17,059 --> 00:02:18,640
Hey, Dad.

23
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:20,820
Yes. Well, anyway,

24
00:02:20,870 --> 00:02:24,620
I hear Kinjirō's older brother works for the police,
is that right?

25
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:25,820
Right? Well,

26
00:02:25,870 --> 00:02:30,060
Calling him an older brother is overstating it,
though. Well.

27
00:02:30,540 --> 00:02:33,860
Your younger son Kinjirō is a fine lawyer,
after all,

28
00:02:33,860 --> 00:02:37,260
so your older son must be a fine police officer too,
I'm sure.

29
00:02:38,540 --> 00:02:41,200
If I recall,
he's the chief of the Katsushika station?

30
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:43,080
Or was he the deputy chief?

31
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:44,280
Oh -

32
00:02:44,280 --> 00:02:45,940
Hey, you.

33
00:02:46,440 --> 00:02:49,260
He's practically guaranteed to become Commissioner General someday,
isn't he?

34
00:02:51,160 --> 00:02:53,420
What a wonderful older brother he is.

35
00:03:00,140 --> 00:03:01,620
Did I really say that?

36
00:03:02,200 --> 00:03:04,800
You don't remember?
What kind of person are you?

37
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:07,180
Don't start remembering! My head's pounding.

38
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:11,220
What are we going to do?
Kankichi's coming to the wedding too!

39
00:03:11,220 --> 00:03:13,960
They've turned him into such a fine,
respectable big brother.

40
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:15,880
Ugh, I'm at my wits' end.

41
00:03:17,700 --> 00:03:20,340
That's it. We just shouldn't
invite Kankichi to the wedding.

42
00:03:20,880 --> 00:03:21,480
You...

43
00:03:23,420 --> 00:03:26,680
If he shows up at the wedding,
it's obvious everything will fall apart.

44
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:29,140
He loves festivals, after all.

45
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:32,560
If he starts doing a naked dance at Iwaizaki,
it'll be a disaster.

46
00:03:33,340 --> 00:03:36,320
The wedding might turn
into a divorce ceremony.

47
00:03:37,100 --> 00:03:39,280
But we can't not let him know, can we?

48
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:40,560
He's his brother, after all.

49
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:43,240
Besides,
he'll be furious if he finds out later.

50
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:44,000
Shut up.

51
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:47,280
If the wedding ends safely,
everything will work out after that.

52
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:50,420
Well, then.

53
00:03:50,940 --> 00:03:52,300
The dismissal is unjust.

54
00:03:53,420 --> 00:03:54,960
You can also claim compensation and damages.

55
00:03:56,760 --> 00:03:58,720
Found it. Thank you very much.

56
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:05,840
Chief, you have a call from your home.
Sorry, excuse me for a moment.

57
00:04:06,900 --> 00:04:12,300
And there were also calls from the Supreme Court General
Secretariat and Diet member Tabuchi of the Minmin Party.

58
00:04:12,740 --> 00:04:13,220
Got it.

59
00:04:17,860 --> 00:04:18,260
Hello?

60
00:04:18,260 --> 00:04:19,180
It's me.

61
00:04:19,180 --> 00:04:20,920
Did you send the wedding invitations?

62
00:04:21,340 --> 00:04:22,680
I sent them this morning.

63
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:23,200
What?

64
00:04:23,840 --> 00:04:25,100
Did you get them postmarked today too?

65
00:04:25,100 --> 00:04:26,720
Of course I did.

66
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:28,420
Damn, was it too late?

67
00:04:28,420 --> 00:04:29,700
Anyway, Dad...

68
00:04:29,700 --> 00:04:32,140
Yesterday you spoke about
big brother like that...

69
00:04:33,100 --> 00:04:33,820
Dad.

70
00:04:34,260 --> 00:04:35,060
Dad.

71
00:04:38,180 --> 00:04:38,980
Dad.

72
00:04:38,980 --> 00:04:39,320
Damn it.

73
00:04:40,240 --> 00:04:41,180
Wait a minute.

74
00:04:41,180 --> 00:04:42,880
If you sent it this morning, then...

75
00:04:43,220 --> 00:04:44,340
it'll arrive tomorrow.

76
00:04:55,480 --> 00:04:57,820
If only the invitation doesn't reach them,

77
00:04:57,820 --> 00:04:59,820
the wedding will be ruined.

78
00:05:06,620 --> 00:05:08,060
It's already past nine.

79
00:05:08,060 --> 00:05:09,400
He still hasn't gone to work?

80
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:10,100
Did he screw up?

81
00:05:12,400 --> 00:05:13,760
Another marital spat?

82
00:05:13,760 --> 00:05:16,600
Yeah, my old lady's being so unreasonable.

83
00:05:16,600 --> 00:05:18,180
Smack, smack, smack!

84
00:05:18,180 --> 00:05:18,980
Did you hit her?

85
00:05:19,520 --> 00:05:20,760
She hit me back instead.

86
00:05:20,760 --> 00:05:23,060
How pathetic.

87
00:05:23,060 --> 00:05:24,620
Shouldn't it be me?

88
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:28,240
Hey, old man.

89
00:05:28,240 --> 00:05:31,460
What are you doing here?

90
00:05:31,460 --> 00:05:34,080
No, I was just doing my
keirin predictions over there.

91
00:05:34,080 --> 00:05:34,980
Hold on a second.

92
00:05:35,780 --> 00:05:36,500
What is it?

93
00:05:37,820 --> 00:05:38,760
Think they found out?

94
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:46,280
Race 11 is a showdown
between Kamioka and Yoshiyama.

95
00:05:46,280 --> 00:05:47,900
Just this one point, the outside is fine.

96
00:05:48,380 --> 00:05:49,360
Hello.

97
00:05:50,260 --> 00:05:50,900
Well, then.

98
00:05:54,720 --> 00:05:55,640
You gave me a scare.

99
00:05:56,980 --> 00:05:57,340
Hey.

100
00:05:58,020 --> 00:05:59,980
W-what is it?

101
00:05:59,980 --> 00:06:01,020
As for Race 10...

102
00:06:01,020 --> 00:06:03,180
You don't have to go to work, do you?

103
00:06:04,040 --> 00:06:04,940
I see.

104
00:06:04,940 --> 00:06:06,920
The Chief should be showing up soon.

105
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:07,460
Alright.

106
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:10,560
What a brazen guy.

107
00:06:13,760 --> 00:06:14,780
Hey, that's enough already!

108
00:06:16,300 --> 00:06:17,620
What's the big idea all of a sudden?

109
00:06:18,580 --> 00:06:19,580
Pardon me.

110
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:35,640
Found it.

111
00:06:37,080 --> 00:06:39,560
As long as this is taken care of,
Kankichi can't come.

112
00:06:42,180 --> 00:06:44,860
Now we can go to the keirin
track with peace of mind.

113
00:06:47,500 --> 00:06:48,880
A touring trip?

114
00:06:48,880 --> 00:06:51,880
Yeah, Honda and Otohime are going along too.

115
00:06:51,880 --> 00:06:54,020
Sounds fun. When is it?

116
00:06:54,020 --> 00:06:55,400
This coming Sunday.

117
00:06:55,400 --> 00:06:59,260
Sorry, I have a wedding that day.

118
00:06:59,260 --> 00:07:02,380
Forget about that. Whose wedding is it?

119
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:06,100
It's my mother's side. My grandmother's
younger sister's son's wife's...

120
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:08,300
...niece,
the daughter of my nephew's older sister.

121
00:07:09,560 --> 00:07:13,340
I don't quite follow, but if they're such distant relatives,
they don't need to attend, right?

122
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:16,620
Well, yes. Maybe I'll just decline.

123
00:07:17,640 --> 00:07:19,500
That's right. I think the invitation is...

124
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:22,220
Found it. What's the phone number?

125
00:07:22,520 --> 00:07:26,660
Kiritani Keiko? That's an unusual surname.

126
00:07:27,380 --> 00:07:28,520
What about the Hana Mukōko side?

127
00:07:29,380 --> 00:07:32,820
Ryotsu Kinjirō. That's unusual too.

128
00:07:33,520 --> 00:07:36,340
Apparently he's a lawyer who
graduated from Tokyo University.

129
00:07:36,340 --> 00:07:40,200
Tokyo University And his
address is in Taito ward?

130
00:07:41,080 --> 00:07:42,700
Is something the matter?

131
00:07:42,720 --> 00:07:46,500
My younger brother also went to Tokyo
University and works as a lawyer in Taito ward.

132
00:07:46,500 --> 00:07:49,440
That's the same as this
Ryotsu Kinjirō person.

133
00:07:49,440 --> 00:07:51,480
What a coincidence.

134
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:55,680
Still, what an unusual surname. Ryotsu Kin?

135
00:07:56,240 --> 00:08:00,860
Ryotsu-sama, couldn't that
possibly be read as Ryotsu Kinjirō?

136
00:08:02,500 --> 00:08:04,160
Ryotsu Kinjirō

137
00:08:04,160 --> 00:08:07,260
So that's it. Ryotsu Kinjirō

138
00:08:07,780 --> 00:08:10,340
Maybe he's a distant
relative of your senior.

139
00:08:12,660 --> 00:08:14,160
He's my younger brother.

140
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:16,020
No way.

141
00:08:16,020 --> 00:08:19,060
Even though he's your brother,
there's no way you wouldn't know, senior.

142
00:08:19,060 --> 00:08:21,520
So it's read "Ryotsu Kin," right?

143
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:23,520
No, this address is definitely right.

144
00:08:23,520 --> 00:08:24,140
Then...

145
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:27,400
Kinjirō didn't tell us anything.

146
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:28,560
Damn it!

147
00:08:30,100 --> 00:08:31,280
Lord Ryo

148
00:08:34,160 --> 00:08:36,100
Things are about to get serious, I'm afraid.

149
00:08:36,920 --> 00:08:37,920
Nakagawa-san.

150
00:08:38,480 --> 00:08:39,520
Nakagawa-san?

151
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:43,800
My senpai and I are
going to become relatives.

152
00:08:45,720 --> 00:08:46,860
That Kinjirō guy!

153
00:08:47,480 --> 00:08:49,060
Why didn't anyone tell me?!

154
00:08:49,720 --> 00:08:50,720
Unforgivable!

155
00:08:51,880 --> 00:08:53,940
What is this,
a chill just ran down my spine.

156
00:08:54,420 --> 00:08:55,760
Got it now!

157
00:08:57,460 --> 00:08:58,840
Get me something to eat, food.

158
00:08:58,840 --> 00:09:01,240
Yes, yes, I'll get it ready right away.

159
00:09:05,320 --> 00:09:06,500
Hey, is dinner not ready yet?

160
00:09:06,500 --> 00:09:10,200
What's the matter with you?
Where did you get this invitation?

161
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:14,620
I borrowed it from
Kankichi Ryotsu's mailbox.

162
00:09:14,620 --> 00:09:16,740
You really are something else.

163
00:09:18,300 --> 00:09:19,020
Hey, dinner!

164
00:09:21,120 --> 00:09:22,000
Hey, dinner!

165
00:09:23,260 --> 00:09:24,180
Takuma

166
00:09:28,380 --> 00:09:29,060
Kankichi

167
00:09:29,060 --> 00:09:31,260
Mrs. Ryotsu's mother.

168
00:09:31,260 --> 00:09:33,380
Maria-chan, what about Kankichi?

169
00:09:34,160 --> 00:09:34,620
Well, that's just...

170
00:09:40,300 --> 00:09:43,020
I was sure it was around here...

171
00:09:44,040 --> 00:09:45,480
There it is!

172
00:09:47,940 --> 00:09:50,700
My uncle will give the guest speech for us.

173
00:09:50,920 --> 00:09:54,220
Next is my junior high school teacher...

174
00:09:56,320 --> 00:09:57,140
Who is that?

175
00:09:57,480 --> 00:09:58,500
It's me! Let me in!

176
00:09:58,760 --> 00:09:59,260
Big brother!

177
00:10:01,260 --> 00:10:02,120
Hey, big brother.

178
00:10:02,600 --> 00:10:03,680
Hey, Kinjirō.

179
00:10:04,040 --> 00:10:05,640
Calm down, big brother.

180
00:10:07,160 --> 00:10:09,100
Pleased to meet you, big brother.

181
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:11,860
Big brother, this is Keiko Kiriya.

182
00:10:12,220 --> 00:10:13,880
We're here today to go over
the wedding arrangements,

183
00:10:14,260 --> 00:10:17,140
what do you mean by not
inviting me to the wedding?

184
00:10:17,860 --> 00:10:21,220
Keiko's mother's younger sister's uncle's

185
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:23,160
I forgot.

186
00:10:23,160 --> 00:10:27,540
Nakagawa, a distant relative,
got his invitation just fine,

187
00:10:27,540 --> 00:10:29,100
but I didn't get mine!

188
00:10:29,860 --> 00:10:31,040
That can't be right.

189
00:10:32,120 --> 00:10:33,260
We sent it to Nikoniko Dormitory.

190
00:10:33,260 --> 00:10:34,380
Don't lie!

191
00:10:34,720 --> 00:10:36,760
I don't know how important you've become,

192
00:10:36,760 --> 00:10:39,840
but I'm such a useless older brother

193
00:10:39,840 --> 00:10:41,040
that I wasn't even invited
to my own brother's wedding!

194
00:10:41,420 --> 00:10:42,740
It's a misunderstanding, big brother!

195
00:10:42,740 --> 00:10:45,120
Then why didn't you send me an invitation?!

196
00:10:45,380 --> 00:10:48,180
I've never felt sadder than I do today.

197
00:10:48,180 --> 00:10:50,500
If it's the wedding of my only brother,

198
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:53,260
I was going to celebrate it no matter what!

199
00:10:53,900 --> 00:10:55,140
I told you, it's a misunderstanding!

200
00:10:55,140 --> 00:10:58,440
That's right!
The invitation was sent properly...

201
00:10:58,440 --> 00:10:59,680
You, move out!

202
00:11:02,400 --> 00:11:03,000
Keiko-san

203
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:07,240
Are you all right, Keiko?

204
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:09,380
Yes, I just stumbled a little.

205
00:11:09,900 --> 00:11:12,740
What a thing to do!
I'm sorry my brother is so rough.

206
00:11:13,260 --> 00:11:14,760
Sorry for being such a rough brother

207
00:11:14,760 --> 00:11:18,600
Since we're at it,
I'll ruin your wedding too.

208
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:21,200
That's just like you, big brother.

209
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:24,620
Whenever I try to grab a little happiness,
you always get in the way.

210
00:11:25,320 --> 00:11:25,880
What did you say?

211
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:30,120
Back in elementary school,
when I first fell for a girl,

212
00:11:32,420 --> 00:11:33,640
"Get closer together!"

213
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:38,260
you took a commemorative photo
right in front of the futon I'd wet.

214
00:11:38,260 --> 00:11:40,600
My first crush was ruined because of it.

215
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:43,240
It's your fault for wetting the bed,
isn't it!

216
00:11:43,740 --> 00:11:45,040
That's not all, you know.

217
00:11:45,620 --> 00:11:47,660
And then there was the time the university
acceptance results came out, too.

218
00:11:53,920 --> 00:11:54,640
Big brother

219
00:11:58,560 --> 00:12:00,860
the two days until the
acceptance notice arrived

220
00:12:02,120 --> 00:12:02,640
Did you feel that way?

221
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:05,460
Thanks to that,
your joy must have doubled, right?

222
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:08,120
That's enough! Just go home!

223
00:12:08,240 --> 00:12:08,840
What?

224
00:12:09,060 --> 00:12:09,880
Kinjirō-san!

225
00:12:10,360 --> 00:12:12,680
It's fine, big brother's just like this.

226
00:12:12,680 --> 00:12:14,900
Oh, I see, I see!

227
00:12:15,020 --> 00:12:17,780
You're no brother of mine,
and I'm no brother of yours!

228
00:12:18,500 --> 00:12:19,100
See ya!

229
00:12:37,060 --> 00:12:37,940
Big brother

230
00:12:38,960 --> 00:12:41,760
Kinjirō, are you really going
to let him leave like this?

231
00:12:42,180 --> 00:12:43,160
Kinjirō...

232
00:12:43,680 --> 00:12:45,880
I'm sick of hearing about that guy.

233
00:13:01,680 --> 00:13:02,460
Kinjirō.

234
00:13:05,740 --> 00:13:06,680
Shirohige Bridge

235
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:10,200
I have memories at Shirohige Bridge.

236
00:13:11,820 --> 00:13:15,580
That was before I started
elementary school, right?

237
00:13:16,140 --> 00:13:17,360
I was watching a kamishibai picture show.

238
00:13:18,360 --> 00:13:21,000
That day, my big brother wasn't around,
so I was alone by chance

239
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:29,040
and I just followed the kamishibai man

240
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:43,100
when I suddenly realized I'd ended
up in a totally different town.

241
00:13:47,340 --> 00:13:49,080
I had no idea how to get back at all.

242
00:13:51,120 --> 00:13:52,620
I thought I'd end up in Asakusa,

243
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:58,160
but where I arrived was Shirohige Bridge,
the complete opposite of Asakusa.

244
00:13:59,600 --> 00:14:00,480
Hello?

245
00:14:05,480 --> 00:14:07,360
Dad! Mom!

246
00:14:14,100 --> 00:14:14,760
Let's go home.

247
00:14:14,760 --> 00:14:15,380
Coming!

248
00:14:17,720 --> 00:14:18,600
Big brother!

249
00:14:45,040 --> 00:14:45,800
Kinjirō!

250
00:14:47,300 --> 00:14:47,860
Big brother!

251
00:14:54,920 --> 00:14:55,971
You had us worried sick,

252
00:14:56,021 --> 00:14:59,080
and now I can't watch the pro wrestling!

253
00:15:01,580 --> 00:15:03,040
Big brother!

254
00:15:09,100 --> 00:15:14,840
I still haven't forgotten the pounding of your heart and the warmth of your back that day,
big brother.

255
00:15:20,680 --> 00:15:22,440
What a wonderful older brother.

256
00:15:22,880 --> 00:15:27,580
That's why you bought an apartment near Shirohige Bridge,
isn't it, Kinjirō?

257
00:15:28,160 --> 00:15:31,220
Because it's a place full
of wonderful memories for me.

258
00:15:33,520 --> 00:15:37,820
Kinjirō, let's really have your
big brother come to the wedding.

259
00:15:38,260 --> 00:15:38,940
Keiko-san

260
00:15:48,380 --> 00:15:49,500
Big brother!

261
00:15:52,460 --> 00:15:53,180
Big brother.

262
00:15:53,540 --> 00:15:54,300
Big brother.

263
00:15:55,020 --> 00:15:55,980
W-why?

264
00:15:57,260 --> 00:15:59,260
Big brother, I was wrong.

265
00:15:59,840 --> 00:16:02,160
Please, I beg you, come to the wedding.

266
00:16:03,040 --> 00:16:03,600
Please attend.

267
00:16:04,480 --> 00:16:05,200
What is it?

268
00:16:05,200 --> 00:16:07,260
Suddenly changing your tune like that.

269
00:16:07,960 --> 00:16:10,620
You're an irreplaceable big brother to me.

270
00:16:10,620 --> 00:16:11,560
Please.

271
00:16:11,560 --> 00:16:12,940
Please come to the wedding.

272
00:16:12,940 --> 00:16:14,640
I'm asking you too.

273
00:16:17,380 --> 00:16:18,460
You idiot!

274
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:20,860
How can you expect me to just say
"Oh, all right" now?

275
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:23,200
We're not brothers anymore,

276
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:24,480
and you're not my brother either.

277
00:16:26,020 --> 00:16:26,720
Big brother

278
00:16:26,720 --> 00:16:27,880
Big brother

279
00:16:28,880 --> 00:16:29,500
Senpai

280
00:16:29,500 --> 00:16:30,120
Kankichi

281
00:16:30,880 --> 00:16:31,800
Mom

282
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:35,820
This invitation is addressed to me,
isn't it?

283
00:16:35,820 --> 00:16:39,140
Dad pulled it out of
the mailbox at the dorm.

284
00:16:39,140 --> 00:16:39,360
What?

285
00:16:40,560 --> 00:16:44,280
At the engagement ceremony, he made up
some nonsense and couldn't back down, so

286
00:16:44,280 --> 00:16:47,040
That damn old man! I'll never forgive him!

287
00:16:49,620 --> 00:16:51,400
Onii-sama, what about the wedding?

288
00:16:52,080 --> 00:16:56,340
Of course I'm going! As his big brother,
I'll make it the best wedding in all of Japan!

289
00:16:56,540 --> 00:16:59,000
Then that's settled! That's right!
You'd better be prepared!

290
00:17:04,040 --> 00:17:06,180
So you're the rigid older brother?

291
00:17:06,880 --> 00:17:07,520
Thanks for today.

292
00:17:07,520 --> 00:17:09,800
They do call me the Man of Steel, you know.

293
00:17:10,820 --> 00:17:11,740
The pleasure's all mine.

294
00:17:13,180 --> 00:17:14,920
Uncle, the restroom is this way.

295
00:17:15,720 --> 00:17:17,380
Once the ceremony's over,
we're taking pictures, got it?

296
00:17:17,380 --> 00:17:19,320
Get everyone lined up sharp, will you?

297
00:17:19,320 --> 00:17:19,880
Yes.

298
00:17:20,320 --> 00:17:21,500
Keep a close eye on the bell.

299
00:17:21,500 --> 00:17:23,100
Watch out for the gift-money thieves.

300
00:17:23,100 --> 00:17:25,100
The reception desk is this way.

301
00:17:25,100 --> 00:17:26,600
The ceremony starts in ten minutes.

302
00:17:26,600 --> 00:17:28,700
Come on, Grandma, this way, this way.

303
00:17:28,700 --> 00:17:30,560
He's completely taken charge, hasn't he.

304
00:17:31,900 --> 00:17:32,880
Are you ready?

305
00:17:33,860 --> 00:17:35,560
Has everyone gathered?

306
00:17:35,560 --> 00:17:37,120
That's perfect, isn't it.

307
00:17:37,460 --> 00:17:39,380
The bride is beautiful, just wonderful.

308
00:17:39,380 --> 00:17:40,920
Truly a crane in a dung heap.

309
00:17:40,920 --> 00:17:41,440
No way.

310
00:17:42,160 --> 00:17:44,740
I have a favor to ask
during the costume change.

311
00:17:44,740 --> 00:17:47,800
Sure, but what are you planning?

312
00:17:47,800 --> 00:17:50,220
I said I'd make it the best wedding in Japan,
didn't I?

313
00:17:50,220 --> 00:17:51,340
Leave it to me.

314
00:17:54,180 --> 00:17:56,240
Right now,
I am the enemy of the leading role.

315
00:17:56,240 --> 00:17:58,820
and that's what I believe, so to speak.

316
00:18:00,560 --> 00:18:02,340
we are at a point where
things are about to change.

317
00:18:02,840 --> 00:18:04,460
As for politics as well,

318
00:18:04,460 --> 00:18:05,480
Alright, that's enough.

319
00:18:06,100 --> 00:18:08,580
This has run too long,
so I'll wrap it up here.

320
00:18:09,220 --> 00:18:10,420
Alright, thank you for your hard work.

321
00:18:10,900 --> 00:18:14,180
Professor Kuroyama, who is said to
be a sure bet for the next minister,

322
00:18:14,720 --> 00:18:16,400
Who is that guy, anyway?

323
00:18:16,860 --> 00:18:19,540
There's an emcee,
but he's running the whole thing himself.

324
00:18:19,540 --> 00:18:23,280
Maybe we shouldn't have
invited him after all.

325
00:18:23,720 --> 00:18:26,000
Emcee, the next greeting is...

326
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:28,980
It's the groom's older brother,
Kankichi Ryotsu.

327
00:18:32,120 --> 00:18:33,800
Now, a few words from
me as his older brother.

328
00:18:34,260 --> 00:18:35,480
How pompous.

329
00:18:36,120 --> 00:18:38,740
This is exactly why I said
I shouldn't have been invited!

330
00:18:38,740 --> 00:18:40,580
Don't blame me for whatever happens.

331
00:18:41,100 --> 00:18:42,420
Even if you say that...

332
00:18:42,920 --> 00:18:44,780
Now I'm getting worried too.

333
00:18:45,360 --> 00:18:48,920
When my younger brother Kinjirō was a child,
he was always wetting the bed.

334
00:18:48,920 --> 00:18:50,500
He was a hopeless kid.

335
00:18:50,500 --> 00:18:51,980
Brother...

336
00:18:51,980 --> 00:18:55,840
Once he grew up, he seemed to
be made entirely of seriousness,

337
00:18:55,840 --> 00:18:57,340
and became a stiff, rigid stick-in-the-mud.

338
00:18:58,020 --> 00:19:01,640
But from an older brother's point of view,
he's still a foolish younger brother.

339
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:03,860
Aren't you the most foolish one of all?

340
00:19:03,860 --> 00:19:06,700
Please take a look. This is our father.

341
00:19:06,700 --> 00:19:08,880
He really does have the
face of a good-natured man.

342
00:19:08,880 --> 00:19:11,400
He was too kind, so he became a guarantor,

343
00:19:11,980 --> 00:19:15,120
and as a result,
he ended up ruining his shop.

344
00:19:15,940 --> 00:19:16,940
Needless to say.

345
00:19:17,520 --> 00:19:22,040
Our relatives include shrine carpenters, gardeners,
day laborers, tatami makers, professors, and senior officers.

346
00:19:22,040 --> 00:19:25,060
It's a parade of ukiyo-e artists, sumo wrestlers,
swordsmiths, and wind-instrument craftsmen.

347
00:19:25,060 --> 00:19:27,000
Our relatives alone
could build a whole house.

348
00:19:27,580 --> 00:19:30,560
They're all lively, spirited,
down-to-earth poor folks, but

349
00:19:30,560 --> 00:19:34,480
one thing we're proud of is that
none of them has robbed a bank yet.

350
00:19:35,580 --> 00:19:39,960
Also, we have plenty of old geezers and grannies in the family,
led by a 107-year-old at the top.

351
00:19:40,420 --> 00:19:43,880
Since they just zone out and don't think about anything,
they end up living long lives.

352
00:19:46,120 --> 00:19:47,720
Next up is a professor
from a national university.

353
00:19:48,160 --> 00:19:48,700
Please, go ahead.

354
00:19:49,600 --> 00:19:51,940
Loosen your ties and make
yourselves comfortable.

355
00:19:51,940 --> 00:19:52,920
Is that really all right?

356
00:19:52,920 --> 00:19:54,740
Yes, after all, we're all family here.

357
00:19:55,720 --> 00:19:57,420
Everyone, let's loosen our ties.

358
00:19:57,940 --> 00:20:00,900
If you keep eating with your neck choked like this,
the food won't go down well.

359
00:20:02,960 --> 00:20:05,400
Little by little,
it's turning into the senior's pace.

360
00:20:10,600 --> 00:20:11,240
(Applause)

361
00:20:13,220 --> 00:20:15,580
That was a splendid classical performance.

362
00:20:16,100 --> 00:20:20,180
But talking to these inconsiderate two
families is like chanting sutras to a horse.

363
00:20:22,200 --> 00:20:23,760
Nakagawa, come here for a sec.

364
00:20:24,860 --> 00:20:27,620
This young entrepreneur
here is my subordinate.

365
00:20:27,620 --> 00:20:29,220
Go say a quick greeting.

366
00:20:29,720 --> 00:20:32,200
Stall for time,
keep going for three minutes.

367
00:20:32,200 --> 00:20:32,780
Yes.

368
00:20:33,240 --> 00:20:36,520
To think he orders around the young master
of the Nakagawa zaibatsu like that...

369
00:20:38,200 --> 00:20:40,860
My senior and I...

370
00:20:40,860 --> 00:20:42,600
Forget it, I've come up with a plan.

371
00:20:46,140 --> 00:20:47,320
Thank you for your patience.

372
00:20:47,320 --> 00:20:51,120
The bride and groom, now in their
changed attire, make their entrance!

373
00:20:52,120 --> 00:20:54,080
Strong! Strong! Strong!

374
00:20:54,180 --> 00:20:55,780
Strong! Strong! Strong!

375
00:20:55,780 --> 00:20:57,060
Strong! Strong! Strong!

376
00:20:57,200 --> 00:20:58,680
Well, well.

377
00:20:59,120 --> 00:21:00,980
The mikoshi bearers have returned.

378
00:21:01,300 --> 00:21:03,920
The carriers are the rowdy
boys from our neighborhood.

379
00:21:04,640 --> 00:21:06,100
Strong! Strong! Strong!

380
00:21:06,100 --> 00:21:06,840
Strong! Strong! Strong!

381
00:21:06,840 --> 00:21:08,100
Wow, this is amazing, Professor.

382
00:21:08,500 --> 00:21:10,400
Compared to TV and such,
the real thing is different.

383
00:21:10,600 --> 00:21:13,300
Well then, everyone.

384
00:21:13,640 --> 00:21:15,200
To celebrate the happiness
of the two of them,

385
00:21:15,240 --> 00:21:16,180
let's drink up!

386
00:21:17,320 --> 00:21:19,940
That's for the newlyweds and the hosts,

387
00:21:19,940 --> 00:21:21,300
it was supposed to be a bad one, but

388
00:21:21,300 --> 00:21:22,420
Don't say something stupid like that.

389
00:21:22,420 --> 00:21:24,120
Come on, drink, drink!

390
00:21:24,120 --> 00:21:26,980
Let's all drink up every last
drop of the hotel's alcohol!

391
00:21:29,260 --> 00:21:31,280
Were you all right riding on the mikoshi?

392
00:21:32,120 --> 00:21:33,760
Yes, what a fun big brother you are.

393
00:21:34,200 --> 00:21:37,160
From today on,
you really become his big brother.

394
00:21:41,160 --> 00:21:43,500
I'm so glad you're such
a reliable big brother.

395
00:21:44,820 --> 00:21:45,660
Is that so?

396
00:21:46,120 --> 00:21:46,880
I like it.

397
00:21:46,880 --> 00:21:49,520
I'll handle all the
renovations on your house myself.

398
00:21:49,940 --> 00:21:51,160
No, that one's definitely there!

399
00:21:51,520 --> 00:21:54,980
Kiriya-san, I look forward to
working with you in the future as well.

400
00:21:55,080 --> 00:21:56,360
No, the pleasure is all mine.

401
00:21:56,660 --> 00:21:59,140
Old man, let's drink ourselves silly today!

402
00:21:59,980 --> 00:22:01,520
It's Hisha-kun.

403
00:22:02,200 --> 00:22:03,900
Ugh, what a hassle.

404
00:22:05,460 --> 00:22:07,060
I'm going to drink way too much today.

405
00:22:13,760 --> 00:22:15,520
Professor, please wake up.

406
00:22:16,740 --> 00:22:18,020
I can't drink anymore.

407
00:22:19,940 --> 00:22:27,900
But I get it, I get it, I'm going to conquer the world, old man!
Our relatives are all wiped out too, boss, are you alright?

408
00:22:27,900 --> 00:22:35,260
Dad, I'm sorry. My brother went overboard with the joking and turned the ceremony into this.
Kinjiro-kun, yes.

409
00:22:36,300 --> 00:22:45,020
I've attended many weddings, but this is
the first one that's been this fun and warm.

410
00:22:45,480 --> 00:22:46,700
What a great older brother.

411
00:22:50,060 --> 00:22:51,200
Kinjiro-kun.

412
00:22:51,200 --> 00:22:51,780
Yes.

413
00:22:52,760 --> 00:22:55,880
Please take good care of my daughter.

414
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:57,440
Yes.

415
00:22:57,900 --> 00:22:58,880
Father.

416
00:22:59,500 --> 00:23:00,080
Look.

417
00:23:00,080 --> 00:23:03,220
Look at Father's face, so happy.

418
00:23:03,220 --> 00:23:04,480
I've never seen it before.

419
00:23:04,480 --> 00:23:06,920
We should thank your older brother.

420
00:23:07,620 --> 00:23:08,640
Where's big brother?

421
00:23:09,680 --> 00:23:11,360
Mom, where's big brother?

422
00:23:11,360 --> 00:23:13,440
He went home with Dad.

423
00:23:18,180 --> 00:23:18,820
Big brother

424
00:23:22,220 --> 00:23:24,780
Dad, that was a great wedding, wasn't it?

425
00:23:24,780 --> 00:23:26,860
It was the best wedding ever.

426
00:23:27,320 --> 00:23:29,300
There were times I thought it'd fall apart.

427
00:23:30,320 --> 00:23:32,880
Kankichi, stay over tonight.

428
00:23:33,820 --> 00:23:34,540
Yeah, I guess.

429
00:23:35,380 --> 00:23:36,860
There's plenty of sake.

430
00:23:36,860 --> 00:23:39,240
And there's the sea bream
they served at the venue.

431
00:23:39,600 --> 00:23:41,600
Bring over everything you left behind.

432
00:23:42,040 --> 00:23:44,020
If that's settled, let's head home quickly.

433
00:23:45,020 --> 00:23:45,220
Here we come.

434
00:23:47,480 --> 00:23:50,000
Kinjirō, be happy.

435
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:52,480
Kankichi, what are you doing?

436
00:23:53,740 --> 00:23:55,180
Right, let's drink!

437
00:23:55,180 --> 00:23:58,900
We're drinking till morning?
At our age, you sure we'll be okay?

438
00:23:58,900 --> 00:24:01,380
I'm not losing to you yet.

439
00:24:15,320 --> 00:24:23,700
Surprise and noise, with spirit,
resolved and swiftly erased,

440
00:24:23,700 --> 00:24:35,360
decided, inspired, bouncing,
gathered, in action and flying away,

441
00:24:36,240 --> 00:24:40,060
above all, an incredible power.

442
00:24:40,060 --> 00:24:52,360
Everyone gather!
Come here, and the dreamlike final energy.

443
00:24:53,380 --> 00:25:03,500
Gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday, drawing the universe,
standing on the ground, it's the same as the star of Kameari coming.

444
00:25:05,540 --> 00:25:07,140
This should be fine, right?

445
00:25:07,140 --> 00:25:08,680
As if it's fine!

446
00:25:21,780 --> 00:25:25,400
Phew, my younger brother Kinjirō's
wedding has also ended safely.

447
00:25:25,400 --> 00:25:28,720
And I've officially become
a relative of the Nakagawas.

448
00:25:28,720 --> 00:25:32,320
From now on, as family,
I'll help boost the Nakagawa Group

449
00:25:32,320 --> 00:25:34,300
and keep making lots of money!

450
00:25:34,700 --> 00:25:37,420
Next time,
treat me well as family, all right?

451
00:25:42,320 --> 00:25:43,720
Thank you for watching.

